This product introduces the following MCP design patterns:
  - Attribution scar: tickets created without requester_email are owned by
    the service account, not the customer — a permanent, auditable record
    that the AI agent made the wrong call.
  - describe_server: a first-call discovery tool that tells a model the auth
    mode, the scopes it holds, its rate-limit budget, and every tool — so it
    can ask "what do you need from me?" instead of guessing and retrying.
  - Naive mode: a demo toggle that strips actionable error guidance down to a
    bare 403, illustrating the retry-loop failure mode of opaque denials.
  - Tool-scope enforcement: per-tool auth overrides, tool gates, and the
    read / write / pii scope hierarchy.

